benchmarks/subset/ulr_vs_pulr -- the 100 programs of [1] ULR-Baseline vs P-ULR for --subset
============================================================================================

A random subset of benchmarks/ulr_vs_pulr (Table 1), on which scripts/run_full_evaluation.sh
--subset runs [1]. The files are unchanged copies of programs of benchmarks/ulr_vs_pulr.

How they were drawn: uniformly at random, with a fixed seed, from the 2,860 programs of the
paper's ULR vs P-ULR run (logs/ULR_vs_PULR_logs.zip, one *.ultimate.log per program):
55 of its 1,559 C programs and 45 of its 1,301 Boogie programs, the proportions of the paper. In
Python 3:

    rng = random.Random(2027)
    c   = rng.sample(sorted(c_programs), 55)
    bpl = rng.sample(sorted(bpl_programs), 45)

The columns give the paper's result for each program, from that same run
(tools/UAutomizer-linux, timeout 3,000 s): the verdict Ultimate reached, the time it took (from
the timestamps of its log) and the number of lasso traces it dumped. ERROR means that Ultimate
stopped on an exception, TIMEOUT that it was killed at 3,000 s; both leave the traces dumped until
then. The 6 programs above 300 s are those that --subset, with its 300 s timeout, stops earlier
than the paper did.

